    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a tool I use to solve problems—whether it’s balancing finances for my freelance business or analyzing data in my photography projects. It’s practical but not inherently exciting; I prefer art and biology more, so math stays in the background unless needed. My parents didn’t have formal education, so I learned through trial-and-error, which made it feel less intimidating.",
